      ],
      "text": "TB infection:",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        133.1956024169922,
        115.38239288330078,
        527.4254150390625,
        129.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "a state of persistent immune response to stimulation by  antigens with  M. tuberculosis",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        129.3824005126953,
        527.4124755859375,
        143.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "no evidence of clinically manifest active TB disease. Most infected people have no signs or symptoms",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        143.3824005126953,
        527.4224243164062,
        157.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "of TB but are at risk for TB disease. This was previously referred to as latent TB infection (LTBI) but",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        157.3824005126953,
        527.3795166015625,
        171.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "given that infection cannot always be considered latent the term TB infection (TBI) is being used",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        171.3824005126953,
        524.3952026367188,
        185.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "instead. There is no gold standard test for direct identification of   infection in humans. M. tuberculosis",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        199.27239990234375,
        224.17088317871094,
        213.6273956298828
      ],
      "text": "TB preventive treatment (TPT):",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        224.17269897460938,
        199.3824005126953,
        527.441650390625,
        213.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "treatment offered to individuals who are considered at risk of TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        213.3824005126953,
        527.4244995117188,
        227.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "disease in order to reduce that risk. Also referred to as treatment of TB infection, LTBI treatment or",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        227.3824005126953,
        175.4453125,
        241.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "TB preventive therapy.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        255.27239990234375,
        204.4611053466797,
        269.62738037109375
      ],
      "text": "Universal health coverage:",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        204.46560668945312,
        255.3824005126953,
        527.3970336914062,
        269.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "under universal health coverage, individuals and communities have",
